347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (Climate change is causing higher temperatures and more frequent extreme weather events, threatening human lives, infrastructure, and ecosystems. Problems like heat waves, melting ice caps raising sea levels, severe storms, floods, and droughts are all linked to rising temperatures. To address these issues, we need sustainable methods to reduce our carbon footprint, lessen negative impacts, and move toward a carbon-free economy.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (Fighting climate change is crucial for meeting sustainable development goals, protecting ecosystems, and ensuring fair access to resources and opportunities for everyone. Vulnerable communities are especially harmed, and social inequalities are worsened. Climate change also poses serious health risks, like heat-related illnesses, diseases spread by insects, and food insecurity. By reducing carbon emissions and promoting sustainable practices, we can improve air quality, boost food security, and protect public health. Building resilience to climate impacts involves investing in sturdy infrastructure, early warning systems, and disaster preparedness to minimize damage from extreme weather. Cooperation among nations, businesses, and society is essential to create tools that help everyone monitor their environmental impact and adopt sustainable practices.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
