382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 306 0 R
/E (Addressing climate change involves many groups with different interests. Governments create and enforce policies to reduce emissions and promote renewable energy, affecting businesses, communities, and individuals. NGOs, advocacy groups, and grassroots movements raise awareness and push for policy changes, often representing marginalized communities who are most affected by climate change.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 306 0 R
/E (Local communities in vulnerable areas, such as coastal regions and small islands, face direct impacts like rising sea levels and severe weather. Indigenous peoples, with their deep connection to the land, are especially affected. Young people are demanding more action on climate change since they will face the long-term effects of today's decisions. Considering the views of all these groups is essential for effective climate strategies. Working together can lead to balanced solutions that address environmental, social, and economic needs.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
